      "retweet": {
        "id": "2060040473566163377",
        "text": "The trial has concluded, the facts have been confirmed. As the prosecuting counsel put it, Digwa used his “trump card” by alleging he had been the victim of racist abuse when police officers arrived. \nDEI has again proved lethal - literally lethal. Henry Nowak, like the victims of Valdo Kalocane, of Axel Rudakubana, of the rape gangs, was failed by a public sector that treats anti-racism as its supreme value. \nUnlike the death of George Floyd, his death plainly did reveal institutional bias - a bias deliberately cultivated across state bodies by years of training sessions and seminars. \nWhere are the protests? Where are the knee-takings? Where are the corporate boycotts? \nSod it, let’s be more modest. Is anyone even calling for an overhaul of the police?",
        "created_at": "Thu May 28 16:48:17 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "media": [],
        "retweet": null,
        "quoted": {
          "id": "2057796631429316982",
          "text": "“Why the asymmetry in coverage? Both men died after being restrained by the police. Nowak’s last words, like Floyd’s, were reported to be ‘I can’t breathe’. Yet there have been no riots  over the white victim, no statues smashed, no corporate vigils. No one has been fired for saying that all lives matter.\nIndeed, until @elonmusk took an interest, Nowak’s death was being reported as a local crime story.”\nhttps://t.co/z6kllFtvZ9",
